# Build context for backend/Dockerfile is the repo root. Keep it to what the image needs.

# Secrets: never send any .env file to the Docker daemon (or into an image layer).
**/.env
**/.env.*

.git
.github

# Python
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.hypothesis
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov

# Node (the frontend has its own image and .dockerignore)
**/node_modules
**/dist
frontend

# Not needed at runtime. The seed reads data/cms/; the pipeline that builds it and its
# raw downloads (hundreds of MB) stay out of the image.
data/raw
backend/pipeline
backend/tests
docs
db
**/*.md
